course: dictionary
lesson: 7978
title: Recommendation: advice, suggestions and letters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A recommendation is advice about what to do, or a suggestion that something is good. It often comes from someone who knows, like a doctor or a friend. «The doctor's recommendation is rest» means the doctor advises you to rest.
explain: Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «On someone's recommendation» means because someone suggested it, so «I read the book on my friend's recommendation» means my friend told me it was good. Check by swapping in advice or suggestion and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word also has a formal meaning. «A letter of recommendation» says good things about a person who is applying for a job or a school place. The same word is used, but the words around it tell you which meaning is in use.
explain: Apps and websites make recommendations too. «Recommendation systems learn from what you click and watch, and show you more of it.» The computer suggests things it thinks you will like, based on what you have already done.
fact: A recommendation is advice about what to do, or a suggestion that something or someone is good.
fact: «On someone's recommendation» means because someone suggested it.
fact: «A letter of recommendation» is a letter that says good things about a person applying for a job or school.
fact: Recommendation systems are computer programs that suggest videos, music and other things based on what you click and watch.
fact: «Recommendations may push videos that keep people watching, including angry or scary ones.» So a suggestion from a computer is not always a good one, and it is worth thinking before you follow it.
exercise: «The doctor's recommendation is rest.» What does recommendation mean here? | *Advice about what to do | A letter to the hospital | A kind of medicine | A bill to pay
exercise: «I read that book on my friend's recommendation.» Why did the person read it? | Because it was the only book in the room | Because the school made them | *Because a friend suggested it | Because it was very long
exercise: «A letter of recommendation» says what about a person? | Their shoe size | *Good things, for a job or school | Their address and phone number | Bad things they did last week
test: «Music apps use recommendation algorithms built from your own listening history.» What do these recommendations do? | Sell you a new phone | Write the lyrics for you | Stop the music when you feel tired | *Suggest songs you may like, based on what you have listened to
test: Why might a recommended video keep you watching, even if it is angry or scary? | Because the screen goes dark | Because it is always the shortest video | Because it is always about maths | *Because it is chosen to hold your attention
exam: In «Recommendations may push videos that keep people watching», what does push mean? | *Show you more, often without you asking | Pick up and carry | Stop and wait | Delete for ever
